 for the ordinal variables, affect the resulting correlation structure. The analysis focuses on discrete uniform margins and margins with decreasing probabilities, with varying number of categories.\n\n#### References\n\nMolenberghs, G.; Lesaffre, E. 1994: Marginal modeling of correlated ordinal data using a multivariate Plackett distribution Journal of the American Statistical Association 89(426): 633-644\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.unimi.it/en/ugov/person/alessandro-barbiero)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;   * Latent t Models for Ordinal Data: Likelihood Inference beyond the Multivariate Normal / A. ...   * Simulating correlated ordinal data via the multivariate Student’s t distribution / A.\n\n  * Statistics\n\n### A.Y. 2024/2025\n\n  * Labour Statistics\n\n  * Statistical Methods for Finance\n\n  * Statistics\n\n### A.Y. 2023/2024\n\n  * Labour Statistics\n\n  * Statistical Methods for Finance\n\n  * Statistics\n\n### A.Y. 2022/2023\n\n  * Labour Statistics\n\n  * Statistical Methods for Finance\n\n  * Statistics\n\n### A.Y. 2021/2022\n\n  * Labour Statistics\n\n  * Statistical Methods for Finance\n\n  * Statistics\n\nResearch\n\n### Publications\n\n  * Latent t Models for Ordinal Data: Likelihood Inference beyond the Multivariate Normal / A. Barbiero, A. Hitaj. Optimization : 20-22 July Lisboa 2026.\n\nDettaglio\n\n  * Simulating correlated ordinal data via the multivariate Student’s t distribution / A. Barbiero, A.H. - In: 2025 6th International Conference on Data Analytics for Business and Industry (ICDABI)[s.l] : IEEE, 2026 Jun 09. - ISBN 979-8-3315-6982-2. - pp. 322-326 (( 6. International Conference on Data Analytics for Business and Industry Bahrain 2025 [10.1109/icdabi67967.2025.11547786].\n\nDettaglio\n\n  * A collective risk model with shared latent variable inducing dependence among claim frequency and sizes / A. Barbiero, A. Hitaj. 38. Panhellenic and 4th International Statistics Conference Salonicco 2026.\n\nDettaglio\n\n  * A discrete Kumaraswamy distribution for modeling rating and ranking data / A. Barbiero, A. Hitaj. - In: ENVIRONMENTAL AND ECOLOGICAL STATISTICS. - ISSN 1352-8505. - (2026), pp. 1-32. [Epub ahead of print] [10.1007/s10651-025-00697-z]\n\nDettaglio\n\n  * A new discrete exponential distribution: properties and applications / A. Barbiero, A. Hitaj. - In: JOURNAL OF STATISTICAL THEORY AND PRACTICE. - ISSN 1559-8608. - 19:3(2025 Sep), pp. 39.1-39.24. [10.1007/s42519-025-00447-1]\n\nDettaglio\n\nAll publications on AIR--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAlessandro Barbiero's research works | Università degli Studi di Milano-Bicocca, Milan (UNIMIB) and other places (https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Alessandro-Barbiero-78024370)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; The key properties of the distribution are explored, with a particular focus on the possible shapes of its probability mass function, moments, pseudo-random simulation, and inferential procedures. ... Simulating correlated ordinal data via the multivariate Student’s t distribution\nThis distribution offers an alternative to existing models, such as the discrete Beta, the Beta-Binomial, and the CUB distributions, for modeling ordinal data, which are ubiquitous in applied disciplines. The key properties of the distribution are explored, with a particular focus on the possible shapes of its probability mass function, moments, pseudo-random simulation, and inferential procedures. Regression models where the response variable follows the proposed discrete Kumaraswamy distribution are also discussed. Analyses of different real data sets, regarding individuals’ perspectives on environmental matters, are provided to practically illustrate the model introduced in this work and assess its ability to fit rating or ranking data.\n\n[Button: Read more]\n\nDownload\n\nS